# BYU CCDC tryout, 2026-09-26 - the "Mojank Studios" packet.
# Windows box: lapis, Windows Server 2016 - a domain controller (AD/DNS scored).
#
# Put it where every tool finds it without -Config, from the kit folder:
#     mkdir C:\ProgramData\CCDC -Force | Out-Null
#     copy config\tryout-windows.env C:\ProgramData\CCDC\ccdc.env
#
# No passwords in here, not even the packet's default. They live on paper.

# --- who ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# On a domain controller every account is a domain account. Administrator is the
# built-in; it is not in the packet and not scored, but it cannot be removed.
CCDC_ALLOWED_USERS="Administrator steve alex enderman creeper villager zombie enderdragon irongolem chickenjockey ghast"
CCDC_INTERACTIVE_USERS="steve alex enderman creeper villager zombie enderdragon irongolem chickenjockey ghast"
CCDC_PACKET_PASSWORD=""               # optional; type it in C:\ProgramData\CCDC\ccdc.env on the day

# --- what: a domain controller's scored services and what they stand on ------------
# The scorer does an LDAP login (AD) and DNS lookups. Those need the directory
# (NTDS), Kerberos (Kdc), Netlogon, DNS, and a correct clock (W32Time); AD Web
# Services is what the PowerShell AD cmdlets talk to. If Quotient shows HTTP or
# FTP on this box too, add W3SVC / FTPSVC here and 80 / 21 below.
CCDC_WINDOWS_SERVICES="NTDS DNS Kdc Netlogon ADWS W32Time"

# DNS, Kerberos, RPC endpoint mapper, LDAP, SMB (SYSVOL/NETLOGON), Kerberos
# password change, LDAPS, Global Catalog, and RDP - your only way in: Server
# 2016 has no built-in SSH, and the Proxmox console cannot paste.
CCDC_ALLOWED_TCP_PORTS="53 88 135 389 445 464 636 3268 3269 3389"
CCDC_ALLOWED_UDP_PORTS="53 88 123 389 464"
CCDC_TCP_CHECKS="
ldap|127.0.0.1|389|NTDS
dns|127.0.0.1|53|DNS
"
CCDC_HTTP_CHECKS=""
CCDC_RDP_SCORED="1"                   # not scored, but it is how you reach this box: keep it

# --- rules -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rule 4: every source address must reach public services. Nothing here filters
# by address, and nothing should.

# --- lockout: the usernames are in the packet ------------------------------------
# On a DC this is the DOMAIN policy: a spray of ten wrong passwords locks a
# scored account for this many minutes, and every AD check using it fails.
CCDC_LOCKOUT_THRESHOLD="10"
CCDC_LOCKOUT_DURATION="2"
CCDC_PW_MIN_LENGTH="14"
